<title>GERMANY: German Q2 GDP rises 1.5 percent from Q1.</title>
<headline>German Q2 GDP rises 1.5 percent from Q1.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p>PAN-GERMAN GDP    Q2 96	Q1 96	 Q4 95	Q3 95</p>
<p> qtr/qtr	    +1.5	 -0.5	  unch	 unch</p>
<p> yr/yr		+1.2	 +0.2(+0.3)  +1.0	 +1.7</p>
<p>W.GERMAN GDP</p>
<p> yr/yr		+1.1	 +0.3	  +0.8(+0.7) +1.2(+1.3)</p>
<p>E.GERMAN GDP</p>
<p> yr/yr		+2.6	 -1.2(unch)  +2.7(+4.0) +5.7(+5.6)</p>
<p>NOTE - Quarter-on-quarter figures are adjusted for inflation (1991 prices) and for seasonal and calendar factors.</p>
<p>They are rounded to a half pct point. Yr/yr changes are adjusted for inflation but not seasonal or calendar factors.  </p>
<p>The Office gave the following yr/yr details:</p>
<p>PAN-GERMAN GDP	     Q2 96	 Q1 96</p>
<p> Private consumption     +1.2	  +1.8</p>
<p> Public consumption	+3.6	  +3.1(+3.4)</p>
<p> Capital investment	+0.5	  -0.5</p>
<p> Construction		-1.4	 -13.3(-11.8)</p>
<p> Exports		     +2.5	  +3.0</p>
<p> Imports		     -0.7	  +4.4(+2.4)</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
